WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.524
Text to speech that never leaves your device.

2
00:00:05.024 --> 00:00:09.542
How OpenFile reads text aloud with your system voices, and falls back to

3
00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.555
a small neural voice model that runs in the tab.

4
00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:19.376
System voices first. Every major browser has a Speech Synthesis API that

5
00:00:19.376 --> 00:00:22.861
uses the voices installed on your operating system.

6
00:00:24.663 --> 00:00:27.948
When there are no voices. Some setups have no voices at all.

7
00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:32.864
Pick an engine. You can also choose the engine yourself.

8
00:00:34.665 --> 00:00:39.224
Going the other way. If you need speech turned into text, Audio Transcriber

9
00:00:39.224 --> 00:00:41.108
runs the Whisper model locally.

10
00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.801
To try it, open Text to Speech in OpenFile.

11
00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:49.634
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

12
00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:53.064
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

13
00:00:56.009 --> 00:00:59.700
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
